  "exact_classification": {
    "single_shell": "F_N(t)=b+2*A0*t+t^2=(A0+t)^2-N; the least t>=0 making F_N(t) a square is exactly the Fermat midpoint offset T",
    "factor_ratio": "T=sqrt(N)*(cosh(0.5*log(q/p))-1) - (ceil(sqrt(N))-sqrt(N)); the shell term is a subunit rounding correction, while the macroscopic term is the hidden factor ratio",
    "neighbor_prime": "testing prime candidates downward from floor(sqrt(N)) until p is reached is trial division in a different order; J_p is a factor-labeled diagnostic, not a deployable N-only feature",
